# StateTree Tools (UE 5.6)

This toolset is deliberately bound to the StateTree and GameplayStateTree APIs shipped with Unreal Engine 5.6.1. It does not carry later-engine compatibility branches.

The base `UnrealMCP` plugin does not enable StateTree for the host project. To
use this surface, explicitly enable the UE 5.6 `StateTree` and
`GameplayStateTree` plugins plus the editor-only `UnrealMCPStateTree`
companion plugin in the target project, then restart the editor.

The Python tools remain registered when those plugins are off, but each native
route returns `dependency_plugin_disabled` with `required_plugins` and
`disabled_plugins`. This is a pre-dispatch failure with
`mutation_attempted=false`, `mutation_performed=false`, and `changed=false`;
enable the listed plugins and restart instead of retrying the mutation.

## Tools

- `list_state_trees(directory="/Game", recursive=true, max_results=200, offset=0)`
  - Lists StateTree assets with deterministic bounded pagination.
- `inspect_state_tree(asset_path, max_states=500)`
  - Reads schema, runtime-ready state, compiled hash, and a bounded recursive hierarchy including state IDs, types, task/condition/transition counts, and child states.
- `create_state_tree(name, package_path="/Game/AI/StateTrees", schema_type="component")`
  - Creates an idempotent StateTree with the UE 5.6 GameplayStateTree `component` or `ai` schema, compiles it, and saves it.
  - Creation targets must be project content under `/Game`; engine and plugin content is never mutated.
- `add_state_tree_state(asset_path, state_name, parent_path="Root", state_type="state", selection_behavior="children_in_order", dry_run=true)`
  - Adds a standard child state. Supported types are `state`, `group`, and `subtree`; supported selection behaviors are `none`, `enter`, and `children_in_order`.
  - Nested `parent_path` values use the same `/` separator returned by inspection, for example `Root/Combat`.
  - Apply mode compiles, saves, and independently resolves the new state by path.
  - Apply targets must be under `/Game` and must not have unrelated unsaved changes.
  - `dry_run` must be a JSON boolean; string and numeric lookalikes are rejected
    before dispatch so they cannot accidentally enter apply mode.
- `compile_state_tree(asset_path, save=true)`
  - Runs UE 5.6 validation and compilation and returns compiler messages.
  - Compile/save targets must be project content under `/Game`.

All saved classes are standard StateTree/GameplayStateTree classes. The
companion is an authoring provider only: finished assets must not persist
`/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCPStateTree`, or another MCP-only
reference. Mutating routes perform both in-memory and persisted dependency
audits. After authoring, the UnrealMCP plugins may be disabled or removed while
the UE StateTree plugins remain enabled.

## Deliberate limits

- No arbitrary task/condition struct injection, property binding editor, or later-engine runtime data surface in this pass.
- No UE 5.7/5.8 API or compatibility branch.
